# AgroTech agent rules

Read `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `docs/setup.md` and `docs/agents/architecture.md`
before changing code. Follow the repository's spec-first flow and use the
existing JavaScript/Express architecture; do not introduce a framework,
bundler, database, ORM or dependency without an explicit decision.

Before implementation, inspect the real callers and contracts. New or changed
API behavior updates `.ai/specs/05-openapi-spec.md`; new business rules need a
test in `tests/`; changes under `src/`, `server.js` or `index.html` update a
spec/task or explain `Spec: n/a — <reason>`.

Use Conventional Commits, never commit or push directly to `main`, and run
`npm run verify` before handing work off. Treat user input as untrusted and
keep tenant/user authorization enforced on the server.
